  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30.3a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30.3a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.3a" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ ofgá man þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þryfealde ordal þus: nime fife ⁊ beo he sylf syxta.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.3a" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ ofga man þæt þrifealde ordal þus: nime fife ⁊ beo sylf sixta.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.3a" corresp="#wit-q">Et inducatur triplex ordalium hoc modo: sumat V et idem sit sextus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30.3a" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ ofgá man þæt ðryfealde ordal ðus, nime fife ⁊ beo him sylf syxta.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And a case which involves the triple ordeal shall be opened as follows: five [compurgators] shall be selected by the accuser and he himself shall make a sixth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und [Kläger] erzwinge (erreiche Inst. H) das dreifache Ordal folgendermassen: er wähle fünf [Eideshelfer] und sei selbst Sechster im [Anklage-]Eide.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let [the plaintiff] compel (obtain, Inst. H) the threefold ordeal as follows: let him take five [oath-helpers] and be himself the sixth in the [accusing] oath.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Cn 22.1a.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
